  "term": "normal-pressure hydrocephalus",
  "definition": "Normal-pressure hydrocephalus is a type of compensated hydrocephalus marked by slowly worsening walking difficulty, declining intellectual function, and urinary incontinence. The spinal fluid pressure is usually in the high-normal range, and it can develop when cerebrospinal fluid absorption is disrupted, such as after subarachnoid hemorrhage or chronic meningitis.",
